    {
      "id": "at://did:plc:hxjt4arn4jpbe6gi6mdinkm4/app.bsky.feed.post/3mzeab7fe622d",
      "handle": "markriedl.bsky.social",
      "display_name": "Mark Riedl",
      "text": "It’d be neat to have a US senator with some understanding of complex systems and agent based modeling.",
      "url": "https://bsky.app/profile/markriedl.bsky.social/post/3mzeab7fe622d",
      "posted_at": "2026-11-02T21:09:05.225Z",
      "likes": 923,
      "replies": 9,
      "reposts": 224,
      "score": 8,
      "score_parts": {
        "engagement": 3.1,
        "recency": 0.6,
        "age_hours": 60.9
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "at://did:plc:flxq4uyjfotciovpw3x3fxnu/app.bsky.feed.post/3mziqgazkbc2x",
      "handle": "emollick.bsky.social",
      "display_name": "Ethan Mollick",
      "text": "AI semiotics: cool paper suggests that AIs are strongly impacted by visual symbols in ways they do not always recognize in their own chains-of-thought. The way they react to those symbols is very different than how a human might interpret them as well. arxiv.org/pdf/2610.364...",
      "url": "https://bsky.app/profile/emollick.bsky.social/post/3mziqgazkbc2x",
      "posted_at": "2026-11-04T16:08:53.537Z",
      "likes": 129,
      "replies": 1,
      "reposts": 17,
      "score": 7,
      "score_parts": {
        "engagement": 2.2,
        "recency": 0.9,
        "age_hours": 17.9
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "at://did:plc:flxq4uyjfotciovpw3x3fxnu/app.bsky.feed.post/3mze7rbg2fc2l",
      "handle": "emollick.bsky.social",
      "display_name": "Ethan Mollick",
      "text": "If this holds up, it is big: \"We asked GPT-6 Astra to edit Qwen3.5-0.8B weights to improve math. It directly changed only 0.016% of weights, fixing 0.8B's reasoning loops & improving math up to 6x and even instruction following 3x, without gradients or training.\" rikiyat.github.io/blog/weight-...",
      "url": "https://bsky.app/profile/emollick.bsky.social/post/3mze7rbg2fc2l",
      "posted_at": "2026-11-02T21:00:10.481Z",
      "likes": 256,
      "replies": 13,
      "reposts": 36,
      "score": 6.9,
      "score_parts": {
        "engagement": 2.5,
        "recency": 0.6,
        "age_hours": 61
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "at://did:plc:flxq4uyjfotciovpw3x3fxnu/app.bsky.feed.post/3mzesndbbxs2l",
      "handle": "emollick.bsky.social",
      "display_name": "Ethan Mollick",
      "text": "Here is a mass attempted replication of old findings of LLMs with new models. Much conventional wisdom is outdated.\n\nRecent models no longer invent citations and both hallucination rates & stereotyping has dropped. But they are still sycophantic & lean left.  zou-group.github.io/llm-claims-s...",
      "url": "https://bsky.app/profile/emollick.bsky.social/post/3mzesndbbxs2l",
      "posted_at": "2026-11-03T02:37:59.273Z",
      "likes": 181,
      "replies": 21,
      "reposts": 29,
      "score": 6.8,
      "score_parts": {
        "engagement": 2.4,
        "recency": 0.7,
        "age_hours": 55.4
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "at://did:plc:6rdthm3ihpqfd7vn2q2ktjrz/app.bsky.feed.post/3mzjsorcdt22y",
      "handle": "markriedl.bsky.social",
      "display_name": "Mark Riedl",
      "text": "One final remark on all of this. I perceive that people are a bit spooked that the LLM can write neural network weights by hand as opposed to by fitting to data. This is taken as evidence of a special capability. But really, the reason people don’t do this is it’s pointless and stupid.",
      "url": "https://bsky.app/profile/markriedl.bsky.social/post/3mzjsorcdt22y",
      "posted_at": "2026-11-05T02:22:06.258Z",
      "likes": 53,
      "replies": 5,
      "reposts": 7,
      "score": 6.6,
      "score_parts": {
        "engagement": 1.9,
        "recency": 1,
        "age_hours": 7.6
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "at://did:plc:zlv6yt7cye6eihhy6cl5gl6g/app.bsky.feed.post/3mziv6j7pme2x",
      "handle": "garymarcus.bsky.social",
      "display_name": "Gary Marcus",
      "text": "local-level midterm referendums restricted data center buildout (whether megawatt cap, zoning, outright ban, etc.) at nearly every opportunity.\n\nai oversight a top issue for incoming dem congress..",
      "url": "https://bsky.app/profile/garymarcus.bsky.social/post/3mziv6j7pme2x",
      "posted_at": "2026-11-04T17:34:02.285Z",
      "likes": 47,
      "replies": 2,
      "reposts": 10,
      "score": 6.3,
      "score_parts": {
        "engagement": 1.8,
        "recency": 0.9,
        "age_hours": 16.4
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "at://did:plc:rrjvo5jwuateqep2i7ih5ckl/app.bsky.feed.post/3mzisiq3hnc2w",
      "handle": "cfiesler.bsky.social",
      "display_name": "Casey Fiesler",
      "text": "I wonder if last night‘s US election results as they relate to AI will finally get through to the folks who have just haven’t been able to accept that not everyone is 100% on board?\n\nI do recognize that a lot of it is specifically data centers which are a narrow slice, but even so!￼",
      "url": "https://bsky.app/profile/cfiesler.bsky.social/post/3mzisiq3hnc2w",
      "posted_at": "2026-11-04T16:46:03.917Z",
      "likes": 26,
      "replies": 1,
      "reposts": 1,
      "score": 5.6,
      "score_parts": {
        "engagement": 1.5,
        "recency": 0.9,
        "age_hours": 17.2
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "at://did:plc:3igkkqe5nkm66olc4y2syzpy/app.bsky.feed.post/3mzj66zveyc2d",
      "handle": "markriedl.bsky.social",
      "display_name": "Mark Riedl",
      "text": "Sure, who has the time and patience? The point is that AI is faster and has infinite patience, so it can do things we would not. That is why we invent software and algorithms. But it's not doing something we didn't know how to do before. It just wasn't worth our time.",
      "url": "https://bsky.app/profile/markriedl.bsky.social/post/3mzj66zveyc2d",
      "posted_at": "2026-11-04T20:15:23.566Z",
      "likes": 1,
      "replies": 1,
      "reposts": 0,
      "score": 4,
      "score_parts": {
        "engagement": 0.6,
        "recency": 0.9,
        "age_hours": 13.7
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "at://did:plc:t2twdzx7kiudzcad7qs4pydf/app.bsky.feed.post/3mz6msnwums24",
      "handle": "garymarcus.bsky.social",
      "display_name": "Gary Marcus",
      "text": "\"In my view, Pope Leo XIV is by far the clearest thinker on AI among prominent world leaders. It was a genuine thrill to meet him yesterday.\"",
      "url": "https://bsky.app/profile/garymarcus.bsky.social/post/3mz6msnwums24",
      "posted_at": "2026-10-31T15:37:37.383Z",
      "likes": 22,
      "replies": 0,
      "reposts": 3,
      "score": 3.8,
      "score_parts": {
